  "body": "The trace guide of #4176 (second part) plans on a new region kind, `KernelRegion::Chains` (`ChainRegion`, `chain_region`). The other kernel stages plan only an area today:\n\n- `entry::stage` refuses a region that is not planar (`NOT_PLANAR`).\n- The law kit (`kit::run`) reads the tool from `planar(...)`.\n\nSo Trace, Engrave on a line, 2D Contour on an open chain and 2D Chamfer cannot run through all the kernel stages yet.\n\nDone means:\n- The entry and exit stage plans an entry for a trace curve on a chain region (air, a plunge or a ramp along the curve), with the same laws as for an area.\n- The order, load and link stages accept a chain region, or refuse it by name where they need an area.\n- The law kit runs a trace case through all stages (L1 to L7).\n\nContext: `docs/decisions/4176-kernel-guides-medial-trace-helix.md` decision 4. Part of #4023 (side branch `side/path-kernel`).\n",
